# Build context exclusions.
#
# Without this the whole workspace — including several hundred megabytes of
# node_modules and the entire git history — is uploaded to the daemon on every
# build, and `COPY packages ./packages` then writes host-built node_modules over
# the ones installed inside the image. Those were built for the host's platform
# and libc; on Alpine they are the wrong binaries.
node_modules
**/node_modules
.git
.github

# Build output. The image builds its own.
dist
**/dist
*.tsbuildinfo

# Test and tooling artefacts.
coverage
test-results
playwright-report
blob-report
e2e/.auth
.turbo

# Local environment and data. A committed secret is bad; a secret baked into an
# image layer is worse, because it survives deletion of the file.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.pgdata
uploads
*.log
*.dump
